      "problem": "Given that $\\frac{{x}^{2}-64}{x-5}=a$ and $\\frac{(x-8)^{2}}{x-5}=b,$ what is $a÷b?$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\na÷b=\\frac{{x}^{2}-64}{x-5}÷\\frac{(x-8)^{2}}{x-5},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}-64}{x-5}÷\\frac{(x-8)^{2}}{x-5} & = \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-64}{x-5}\\cdot \\frac{x-5}{(x-8)^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{(x-8)(x+8)}{x-5}\\cdot \\frac{x-5}{(x-8)(x-8)} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{(x-8)}(x+8)}{\\cancel{x-5}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{x-5}}{\\cancel{(x-8)}(x-8)} & = \\\\ (x+8)\\cdot \\frac{1}{(x-8)} & = \\\\ \\frac{x+8}{x-8}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
